    This knowledge community centers on administrative and contractual requirements for a state group insurance program, likely involving a Division of State Group Insurance and a Department. Key themes include insurance coverage, performance guarantees, communication protocols, service continuity, and compliance.

Important entities include performance bonds, insurance policies, subcontractors, medical plans, and employer group waiver plans (EGWPs) for retirees. A performance bond must remain in effect for two years, with an amount not exceeding twenty percent. Minimum service requirements are detailed in Attachment 2, Performance Guarantees. Subcontractors provide multilingual customer service. The Department must be notified immediately if liability insurance coverage is lost, and adequate insurance satisfactory to the Department is required.

Communication methods include conference calls, telephone calls, and emails, with Darrell Gholar as a contact at the Division of State Group Insurance, reachable at 4050 Esplanade Way, Suite 217D, or via email. Conference calls may include emails and telephone calls. The Division offers assistance that is impartial, technically sound, and objective.

Other provisions address continuity of care, eligibility file transfers, system technical services, mailroom services, and quarterly plan year requirements. Compliance topics include felony considerations, material misrepresentation, Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act, and Section 7.3 exercise. The overall context emphasizes contract administration, insurance compliance, and member services for state employees and retirees.

